ated around 1395 in many modern accounts.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fra_Angelico","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Cultural association · not necessarily the place of creation"},{"id":"t63-f4ce6c639ae9","title":"Battle of Nicopolis","lane":"history","start":1396,"end":1396,"approx":false,"note":"Ottoman victory over a crusading coalition.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Nicopolis","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"year","threads67":["eastmed"],"setting67":"Historical setting"},{"id":"t63-527635617988","title":"Michelozzo","lane":"people","start":1396,"end":1472,"approx":false,"note":"Florentine architect and sculptor.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michelozzo","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Cultural association · not necessarily the place of creation"},{"id":"t63-92ebfe44b8db","title":"Kalmar Union","lane":"history","start":1397,"end":1397,"approx":false,"note":"Denmark, Norway and Sweden.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalmar_Union","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"year","threads67":["shared"],"setting67":"Cross-regional / setting not yet specified"},{"id":"t63-2e6852deed95","title":"Paolo Uccello","lane":"people","start":1397,"end":1475,"approx":true,"note":"Painter; perspective studies.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paolo_Uccello","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Cultural association · not necessarily the place of creation"},{"id":"t63-0adb5445478c","title":"Rogier van der Weyden","lane":"people","start":1399,"end":1464,"approx":true,"note":"Netherlandish painter.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rogier_van_der_Weyden","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["low"],"setting67":"Cultural association · not necessarily the place of creation"},{"id":"t63-828dc43ee450","title":"Limbourg brothers","lane":"people","start":1400,"end":1416,"approx":true,"note":"Pol, Johan and Herman; approximate period of activity, not a lifespan.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limbourg_brothers","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"activity","threads67":["low"],"setting67":"Cultural association · not necessarily the place of creation"},{"id":"t63-e3567bfa0acf","title":"Johannes Gutenberg","lane":"people","start":1400,"end":1468,"approx":true,"note":"Printer; birth approximate.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannes_Gutenberg","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["central"],"setting67":"Historical setting"},{"id":"t63-f1c26075d7bf","title":"Filarete","lane":"people","start":1400,"end":1469,"approx":true,"note":"Antonio Averlino; architect and sculptor.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filarete","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Cultural association · not necessarily the place of creation"},{"id":"t63-73aa689a3d69","title":"Early Italian Renaissance","lane":"art","start":1400,"end":1490,"approx":true,"note":"Editorial period range; artists and cities developed at different rates.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Early_Renaissance","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"period","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical setting","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t69-629eb3ead524","title":"Linear perspective: horizon and vanishing point","lane":"art","start":1400,"end":1500,"approx":true,"note":"Orthogonals converge towards a vanishing point on the horizon in single-point perspective. The horizon corresponds to eye level, not necessarily a visible skyline.","creators":[],"reference":"https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/architecture-in-renaissance-italy","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t69-82191bb0d296","title":"Atmospheric perspective","lane":"art","start":1400,"end":1600,"approx":true,"note":"Distant forms can appear less distinct, lower in contrast and cooler in colour. This differs from the geometric convergence of linear perspective.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Atmospheric%20perspective","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t69-2291145e213a","title":"Centralised plan and Renaissance ideals","lane":"architecture","start":1400,"end":1600,"approx":true,"note":"Circular, square and Greek-cross plans can express geometrical order. A Greek cross has arms of approximately equal length, unlike a longitudinal Latin cross.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Centralised%20plan%20and%20Renaissance%20ideals","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept"},{"id":"t69-2f3c166311ae","title":"Disegno and colore","lane":"art","start":1400,"end":1600,"approx":true,"note":"The traditional comparison contrasts drawing and design associated with Florence with colour and painterly handling associated with Venice. It is a critical framework, not an absolute regional rule.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Disegno%20and%20colore","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t69-55f40d6a5754","title":"Fresco, tempera and oil: identifying technique","lane":"art","start":1400,"end":1600,"approx":true,"note":"Buon fresco uses pigment on fresh plaster; tempera uses an emulsion binder; oil paint dries through oxidation. Support, binder and application are separate questions.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Fresco%2C%20tempera%20and%20oil","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy","low"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t69-9a016773120d","title":"Patronage, guilds and artistic commissions","lane":"history","start":1400,"end":1600,"approx":true,"note":"Churches, civic bodies, rulers, guilds and private patrons commissioned different subjects and formats. A work's purpose can explain its scale, placement and iconography.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Patronage%2C%20guilds%20and%20artistic%20commissions","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept"},{"id":"t69-46c24b5ffb16","title":"Renaissance architectural proportion","lane":"architecture","start":1400,"end":1600,"approx":true,"note":"Architects reinterpreted classical orders, symmetry and measured relationships. Classical appearance can coexist with new construction solutions and Christian functions.","creators":[],"reference":"https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/architecture-in-renaissance-italy","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept"},{"id":"t69-dc5b3770bdf0","title":"Sfumato and chiaroscuro","lane":"art","start":1400,"end":1600,"approx":true,"note":"Sfumato softens boundaries through subtle tonal transitions. Chiaroscuro models form through light and shade. The two terms are related but not interchangeable.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Sfumato%20and%20chiaroscuro","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t63-bb142cb416a6","title":"Masaccio","lane":"people","start":1401,"end":1428,"approx":false,"note":"Florentine painter.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masaccio","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Cultural association · not necessarily the place of creation"},{"id":"t63-2f8e6011094b","title":"Battle of Ankara","lane":"history","start":1402,"end":1402,"approx":false,"note":"Timur defeats Bayezid I.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Ankara","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"year","threads67":["eastmed"],"setting67":"Historical setting"},{"id":"t63-13750798fa37","title":"Leon Battista Alberti","lane":"people","start":1404,"end":1472,"approx":false,"note":"Architect and humanist.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leon_Battista_Alberti","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Cultural association · not necessarily the place of creation"},{"id":"t63-caa6ba40955d","title":"Fra Filippo Lippi","lane":"people","start":1406,"end":1469,"approx":true,"note":"Florentine painter; birth approximate.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filippo_Lippi","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["shared"],"setting67":"Cross-regional / setting not yet specified"},{"id":"t63-557336ee7b2e","title":"Battle of Grunwald / Tannenberg","lane":"history","start":1410,"end":1410,"approx":false,"note":"Polish–Lithuanian victory over the Teutonic Order.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Grunwald","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"year","threads67":["shared"],"setting67":"Cross-regional / setting not yet specified"},{"id":"t63-7362025bdf4d","title":"Domenico Veneziano","lane":"people","start":1410,"end":1461,"approx":true,"note":"Painter; birth approximate.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domenico_Veneziano","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["shared"],"setting67":"Cross-regional / setting not yet specified"},{"id":"t63-51e70c53ca6a","title":"Johannes Ockeghem","lane":"people","start":1410,"end":1497,"approx":true,"note":"Composer; birth approximate.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannes_Ockeghem","sourceSheets":[3637],"sourceMapping":"period context","dateType":"lifespan","threads67":["shared"],"setting67":"Cross-regional / setting not yet specified"},{"id":"t63-3915a807e48c","title":"Très Riches Heures: Limbourg campaign","lane":"art","start":1412,"end":1416,"approx":true